cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite both the paper and this repository."
title: "CIC-Intents: Channel-Invariant, Interpretable and Causally Grounded Intent Detection for Italian Multi-Channel Fraud"
abstract: >
  Fraud detection systems that operate across multiple communication
  channels face a structural obstacle: a model trained on one channel
  rarely survives the move to another. We study this problem in the
  Italian fraud landscape and propose CIC-Intents, a framework that
  combines a 12-intent multi-label taxonomy (IFIT), a Multi-Label
  Supervised Contrastive objective, a kernel MMD regularizer with
  post-hoc channel centering, and a gradient-based causal attribution
  procedure based on Probability of Necessity and Sufficiency.
